  [PASS] 83c the projection dilutes the quadrupole exactly as sin^2(Theta), which is what the analytic projection of a P_2 field predicts -- so a stack of randomly oriented external fields keeps the average factor <sin^2 Theta> = 2/3 and not a random-phase cancellation, PROVIDED the stack is rotated to each lens's own ghat_ext (which is exactly what the committed g_ext vectors make possible)   (quadrupole/sin^2(Theta) = ['0.2124', '0.2104', '0.2066'] at Theta = 90, 60, 30 deg -- constant to 2.8%)

